## Third-party components

meshyy has **no third-party source dependencies**. Every line under `Sources/`
is original work by this project's authors, written against the permitted
sources recorded in `docs/provenance.md`.

This is deliberate. See `CLAUDE.md` §Clean-room policy: a zero-dependency tree
is the cheapest way to keep the licensing claim unambiguous.

### System frameworks (linked, not vendored)

| Component | Vendor | Terms |
|---|---|---|
| Network.framework (QUIC, TLS 1.3, NWPathMonitor) | Apple | Apple SDK licence; system framework, not redistributed |
| Security.framework (SecKey, SecCertificate, sec_identity_t) | Apple | Apple SDK licence; system framework, not redistributed |
| Foundation / Darwin libc (termios, pty, posix_spawn) | Apple | Apple SDK licence; system framework, not redistributed |
| swift-corelibs / Swift standard library | Apple | Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception |

### Build- and test-time only (not linked into shipped binaries)

| Component | Terms |
|---|---|
| swift-testing (bundled with the Swift 6.3 toolchain) | Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception |

### Consumer-side note

`MeshyyKit` is consumed by a+Terminal, which additionally links SwiftTerm (MIT)
and Citadel (MIT). Those are dependencies of the *app*, not of meshyy, and
meshyy does not import them.

## Licence allowlist

CI (`scripts/check-licenses.sh`) fails the build on any dependency whose licence
is not one of: MIT, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, Apache-2.0, ISC,
Apache-2.0-WITH-LLVM-exception.

GPL, AGPL, and LGPL dependencies are prohibited without exception.
